  "source_shape_findings": [
    "Whole footprint is a connected front fork/right wing,rear upper diagonal and straight connector, with original low projecting group and rounded attached stair volumes. It is not a facade-only fragment. X source-right,Ysource-up is an image-Y inversion; no mirrored or compass claim.",
    "Front1F lacks rear upper occupied wing; rear2F bottom is connected to disclosed solid terrain rather than a floating building or invented full exposedB1. Right road-side grade is an approximate wedge, not measured contours. Interior rooms are solid exterior-envelope proxies.",
    "Broad1-2F low annex stops before3F. Lower diagonal4F occupied region is shortened near409; far blank portion is retained as lower3F roof. This is bounded inference from room/door conventions and upper blank roof, not proof of an exact level from mere missing room numbers. Final overlay uses true lower4 solid boundary and3F outline dashed.",
    "Rear5F excludes unnumbered eastern/straight-connector roof; no whole fifth storey across front/right wings. R is registered independently by two matching stair-flight centres approximatelyR→5F(-112.5,-5) pixels,3.91px residual each; no .944 outer-line scale imposed. Full5F roof remains closed under the separately traced steppedR roof/parapet. Roof access height and precise setback construction are approximate.",
    "827 source-left glazing beside near-vertical pale name/support band is retained; no guessed text carving. Lattice has narrow/wide/narrow real grid banks and two round columns through upper two levels, plus two ground porch columns and true recess air. Independent rays establish real holes before an opaque back, not dark texture pretending openings.",
    "828 near right-wing end is consistent with the source long facade receding toward entrance,upper pale end frame and slope. The visible outer corner post was added; opening remains true air and cap supported. This is a bounded end-registration choice,not a unique surveyed side identification.",
    "Initial large triangular material spill was removed by retaining Boolean surface material provenance rather than nearest-centroid reassignment. Remaining small white slanted corner by upper glazing belongs to real sloped-wing top/deck geometry; limited unseen detail is disclosed, not recolored to hide it.",
    "Unknown rear windows/AC/equipment are deliberately unmodeled neutral detail, not copied from the front. Pure editable colors are appearance proxies; no source textures or tile-by-tile photographic reconstruction. All final five renders andthree model-only near/slope views were personally inspected for same-version consistency."
  ],
